[Music]  [Music]  for the last week or so depending on  when i actually get this video out the  pts has been live and open to the player  base to try out the new game mode called  countdown  now before i get into it when i first  heard about the new game mode being made  my heart sank not because i didn't want  any more game modes i mean this is  exactly what the division 2 needs but  because i knew whatever was created  would be absolutely crucified by the  community  people would be expecting the game mode  to change everything to be a new game in  its own right  there has been no single game mode to  date that has changed the overall feel  of the division i can already hear  people screaming out survival and while  i agree survival was fun it wasn't a  game changer  personally i played it enough so that i  understood the mechanics and could  consistently extract after that you'd be  lucky if i played it once every few  months and at this stage i haven't  played it in years  yep that's right sorry splinter shield i  haven't even participated in a survival  saturday one day maybe though i'll  probably be one of the first players  knocked out after all this time  so my expectations around this new mode  were a little lower than most i was  looking forward to something that i  could jump into from time to time like  survival or last stand not something  that will completely change my division  experience  and although it may be a little  lackluster i'm not gonna lie i see a lot  of potential with countdown  as a reminder countdown is a new eight  player pve game mode  two cells of four shd agents are  deployed at a power plant to prevent a  lockdown  there is a 15-minute timer that agents  are working against where they need to  secure the site before it's too late  when a couple of objectives have been  completed the agents can then extract  but this is when a familiar enemy makes  themselves known the hunters  while countdown is intended for eight  players and there is matchmaking you can  start with a smaller group and even run  it solo  however there isn't any scaling down for  smaller teams you will still be taking  on the same difficulty and number of  enemies before i jump into it i'm not  going to go on and on about the bugs and  good god i certainly saw my fair share  of these because as we know this is just  a test server these are to be expected  when i first jumped in i was immediately  greeted by a number of modifiers that  were placed on the screen  these didn't really change much from  game to game but i feel like they're  probably holding back on a few for the  final release  next a giant red 15-minute timer pops up  that sends the whole squad into a panic  realising that there was some urgency  required on our part  we followed the tracker to our first  objective in this sequence we were  greeted by hyenas a fair few of them but  nothing we couldn't mow down quickly we  were then alerted of a high-risk enemy  that is now approaching  like his henchmen before him he was of  little hassle to our now squad of five  someone must have gotten lost from their  other squad and ended up with us  the next location we were sent to had us  meet up with the other sale of agents so  there were now eight of us running  around spamming our weapons this was  over before i could even realize what  was going on there were obviously a few  people in here that had played some  rounds of countdown before because i  knew they were objectives but by the  time i made it to them someone else had  finished it  the objective now was more of a battle  against each other to see who could get  the kills first  we were then given the heads up of the  comms that we've been successful and can  extract  everyone heads over to the marker i was  expecting there to be a few enemies to  wipe as the last push to stop us but i  wasn't expecting the type of enemy we  encountered  suddenly i realized that going in blind  staying away from everyone else's  comments on this game mode may have just  caught up with me  the cockiness that everyone is feeling  after the ease of the first two  encounters mixed with the sudden  introduction of the hunters that have  been hiding within the black tusk ranks  that we were engaging meant that three  of our seven agents one got disconnected  were instantly dropped  we just ran in too fast we didn't have  to worry about the enemies dropping us  before why would this encounter be any  different  at the end of the day we successfully  wiped the black tusk along with the  hunters who were supporting them and  then extracted i can't show you any end  screens because i've been encountering  the known infinite load in screen bug  that can happen after you extract  so did i find it fun  yes absolutely there is something about  the chaos of running around with seven  other agents that really adds to the  game mode  i know this can be achieved with raids  but they're different not because there  isn't matchmaking but because they  require solid communication  countdown works with matchmaking because  the tasks required are a lot more  straightforward plus there is a little  bit of randomness at least through the  number of sessions i've played so far  more than once i came across a random  hunter while moving between objectives  and every time this happened i was  lagging behind my squad  while most of the time i didn't have a  problem dealing with it i did end up  getting separated from my group unable  to find them again  in fact most of the time i ended up  finding the other sale of agents and  just teamed up with them until the two  groups combined later on  is it replayable  like i said earlier i don't really find  any of the game modes in either game all  that replayable and what i mean by that  i couldn't really play any of the  division 1 or 2 game modes over and over  all night i would usually bounce across  a number of them  but i certainly found countdown a lot  more interesting than underground and  especially summit i only managed to  complete this one once and it was more  for completion purposes not because i  was enjoying it  i see a lot of people comparing  countdown to summit i admit the few  objectives we've seen so far are quite  familiar but that's about where the  similarities end  for starters the map is beautiful summit  was just bare bones 101 map construction  the game plan summit is also very static  even where you take cover feels like it  has been predefined  is there any law  from what i could tell no and i don't  expect there to be any going forward  none of the game modes up into this  point have provided much in the way of  law  do i think a pvp element should be added  no but hear me out  pvp survival worked so well because  builds were taken out of the picture  players were forced to use what they  could find or craft later on  bringing pvp into this mode would kill  it straight away the same issues that  plagued the division pvp in conflict and  the dark zone would be present here too  as the majority of players in the  division are not pvp players this would  lead to the game mode being dead on  arrival  they could add a pvp option to the game  mode like in survival but this would  require quite a number of technical  changes in order to make this work  there are so many ways a team could  ignore objectives and ambush the other  team not caring whether they extract or  not  plus the issues around the division and  many other rpgs around pvp balancing  would just end up being another sore  spot among pvp players  i mean this is why heartlands has been  created builds are being taken out of  the picture the balancing issues will be  far easier to handle  i do question the use of the timer i'm  not a huge fan of timers and games  anyway i hate speedruns and i like to be  able to have more options when playing  through content not just the build and  tactics that revolve around killing  things the fastest i tried a few options  and it really just felt like full dps  was really the only way  however in saying that the time was  never really an issue  with every game i played we were in the  extraction zone far sooner than we  needed to be  it was only really a problem when i was  running solo of which i managed to do a  number of times  running a safer build would mean that  you couldn't kill enemies fast enough so  again you're forced to run glass cannon  and other high dps builds  but i imagine this will change when the  difficulty is altered there is no way  they'll be leaving the difficulty as it  currently is  the mode will either be tweaked to hell  so it's more challenging or we will be  given difficulty options when setting up  a new game  because right now it's far too easy for  eight players or even four  the loot drops are fantastic if it stays  as it is and you can continue to select  the type of loop that drops this is the  best place to farm in the game  especially because of the hunters at the  end  i will however say that it's pretty  anticlimactic once you get to the  extraction  once the black tusk and hunters are down  it just kinda ends  pure chaos for five to ten minutes and  then it just stops  but for all we know there could be an  option to carry on to a next phase for  example with increased difficulty  summing up the pros and cons  a player madness is fun half the time i  think i was shooting my fellow agents  because there was so much shooting going  on  matchmaking actually works because of  the simplicity of the objectives  no forced pathing i got lost tons of  times usually ending up with the wrong  team  the map looks great  and of course you get a ton of loot in  the short period of time  cons  the time limit is this really needed  this affects the builds that are viable  same old enemies nothing new  the map although beautiful could become  repetitive  the difficulty is far too easy  and realistically there is nothing  really new it's just like playing a  larger version of a mission except with  eight players and minimal to no story  i have a couple of suggestions that  could improve the experience that may  have already been considered but wasn't  released in the test version  the time limit should go it only takes  away from the experience  add difficulty options  a larger variety of objectives a larger  variety of directives  add a couple more map variations  more random events like the hunters  popping up randomly in the middle of the  map anything that breaks the standard  complete one objective move on to the  second objective kill the hunters in  black task and then extract  add an option to continue into multiple  phases each increasing in difficulty  with the risk of losing countdown  credits that you've gained previously  not that i know what these credits are  actually used for yet  one thing i want to say and i think it's  important to recognize is that sometimes  i and my fellow youtubers can kind of be  dicks sorry guys but it's true we can be  at the end of the day we're simply  giving our opinions as gamers on what we  have experienced and how we feel about  the direction of where the game is going  because of this a few not all but a few  have found a niche where they prefer to  focus directly on the negative side of  things rather than exploring the other  side which in the long run can have  quite a large impact on the community  anger is probably the easiest emotion to  tap into and thus get a reaction from  and because of this it can often lead to  people either coming in with unrealistic  expectations or automatically assuming  the worst  as always i urge you to go in with an  open mind and make your own opinion  i by no means think that countdown is  for everyone and it's true that it  really isn't bringing anything hugely  unique and groundbreaking to the  franchise but i think there will be a  decent chunk of players who will enjoy  this with a few tweaks i'll certainly be  jumping into it from time to time  the other thing that needs to be  remembered is that this is a pts a  number of the smaller problems will be  fixed like difficulty and maybe even the  timer in enemies etc we just need to  wait and see how much of the feedback  the actual constructive feedback that  the dev team takes on board  anyway thank you very much for watching  and i'll catch in the next one cheers  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  uh

